{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-39654","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68420","text":"Forge Semantic IR v1 — FROZEN"}]},{"id":"blk-39655","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68421","text":"*Status: "},{"id":"spn-68422","marks":["bold"],"text":"FROZEN"},{"id":"spn-68423","text":" (2026-07-21), per GPT-5.6 ruling. Profile: "},{"id":"spn-68424","marks":["code"],"text":"forge.world.core.v1"},{"id":"spn-68425","text":" — the "},{"id":"spn-68426","marks":["bold"],"text":"deterministic-circuit-world"},{"id":"spn-68427","text":" profile. This is the sanctioned lowering target for WRL Core 0.1.1. WRL surface text NEVER lowers directly to interaction-calculus text; it lowers to this IR, which lowers to TRVM facts/films/reductions.*"}]},{"id":"blk-39656","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68428","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scope statement (normative)."},{"id":"spn-68429","text":" IR v1 defines static deterministic signal graphs containing the five built-in roles, persistent numeric/pose state, bounded ADMIT claim state, and the two grounded topology relations. It does "},{"id":"spn-68430","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-68431","text":" define mailboxes, arbitrary actor behavior, dynamic topology, fragments, capabilities, supervision, or distributed settlement. Any construct outside this scope MUST produce a clear unsupported-feature diagnostic, never a speculative lowering."}]},{"id":"blk-39657","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68432","text":"Predecessor: "},{"id":"spn-68433","marks":["code"],"text":"FORGE_SEMANTIC_IR_v1_MEASURE.md"},{"id":"spn-68434","text":" (the pre-freeze measure). Frozen core: "},{"id":"spn-68435","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_CORE_0.1.md"},{"id":"spn-68436","text":" (rev 0.1.1). This freeze resolves decisions D1–D5 as ruled."}]},{"id":"blk-39658","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68437","text":"0. Three layers (D3)"}]},{"id":"blk-39659","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68438","text":"IR v1 is three artifacts with three lifetimes. They are never conflated."}]},{"id":"blk-39660","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"ArtifactIR (static)  +  RuntimeState (persistent)  +  EpochInput (per-epoch)\n    → RuntimeState'  +  Observables"},{"id":"blk-39661","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39663","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68439","marks":["bold"],"text":"Static artifact"},{"id":"spn-68440","text":" — durable topology + role configs + policy references + schema references. Content-addressed."}]}],"id":"blk-39662","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39665","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68441","marks":["bold"],"text":"Persistent runtime state"},{"id":"spn-68442","text":" — world state, claim facts, receipts, capacity-fault latches, clock/pose/rotor/fault state. Threads across epochs."}]}],"id":"blk-39664","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39667","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68443","marks":["bold"],"text":"Epoch input"},{"id":"spn-68444","text":" — the incoming claim batch (later: external / effect-wall observations)."}]}],"id":"blk-39666","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-39668","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68445","text":"Claim facts and receipts are "},{"id":"spn-68446","marks":["bold"],"text":"top-level runtime state"},{"id":"spn-68447","text":", not hidden inside a special actor. ADMIT's "},{"id":"spn-68448","marks":["italic"],"text":"policy identity"},{"id":"spn-68449","text":" is static; its "},{"id":"spn-68450","marks":["italic"],"text":"facts and receipts"},{"id":"spn-68451","text":" are runtime state; the incoming "},{"id":"spn-68452","marks":["italic"],"text":"claim batch"},{"id":"spn-68453","text":" is epoch input."}]},{"id":"blk-39669","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68454","text":"1. Node envelope + five built-in roles (D1)"}]},{"id":"blk-39670","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68455","text":"One structural node envelope is frozen:"}]},{"id":"blk-39671","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Node {\n    object_id\n    role                 ; one of the five closed role IDs below\n    static_config        ; role-specific frozen config\n    state_schema_ref     ; semantic state signature (see §3)\n    ports                ; frozen per-role port signature\n}"},{"id":"blk-39672","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68456","text":"The entire executable v1 role registry is these five (closed):"}]},{"id":"blk-39673","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68457","text":"PulserDecl"}]},{"id":"blk-39674","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39676","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68458","marks":["bold"],"text":"static_config:"},{"id":"spn-68459","text":" clock mode "},{"id":"spn-68460","marks":["code"],"text":"(\"periodic\", period, phase)"},{"id":"spn-68461","text":" | "},{"id":"spn-68462","marks":["code"],"text":"(\"once\", epoch)"},{"id":"spn-68463","text":" (period ≥ 1, 0 ≤ phase < period, period < 1e9; epoch in [0,1e6))."}]}],"id":"blk-39675","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39678","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68464","marks":["bold"],"text":"ports:"},{"id":"spn-68465","text":" out "},{"id":"spn-68466","marks":["code"],"text":"sig_out"},{"id":"spn-68467","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-39677","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39680","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68468","marks":["bold"],"text":"state:"},{"id":"spn-68469","text":" clock state (see §3)."}]}],"id":"blk-39679","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39682","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68470","marks":["bold"],"text":"invariant:"},{"id":"spn-68471","text":" fires deterministically by clock mode; never data-dependent."}]}],"id":"blk-39681","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-39683","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68472","text":"RelayDecl"}]},{"id":"blk-39684","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39686","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68473","marks":["bold"],"text":"static_config:"},{"id":"spn-68474","text":" none."}]}],"id":"blk-39685","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39688","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68475","marks":["bold"],"text":"ports:"},{"id":"spn-68476","text":" out "},{"id":"spn-68477","marks":["code"],"text":"sig_out"},{"id":"spn-68478","text":"; in "},{"id":"spn-68479","marks":["code"],"text":"sig_in"},{"id":"spn-68480","text":" (or-merge of incoming wires)."}]}],"id":"blk-39687","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39690","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68481","marks":["bold"],"text":"state:"},{"id":"spn-68482","text":" "},{"id":"spn-68483","marks":["code"],"text":"cur_out"},{"id":"spn-68484","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68485","marks":["code"],"text":"next_out"},{"id":"spn-68486","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-39689","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39692","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68487","marks":["bold"],"text":"invariant:"},{"id":"spn-68488","text":" "},{"id":"spn-68489","marks":["code"],"text":"next_out = OR(incoming .nxt)"},{"id":"spn-68490","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-68491","marks":["code"],"text":"cur_out' = next_out"},{"id":"spn-68492","text":" at commit."}]}],"id":"blk-39691","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-39693","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68493","text":"DoorDecl"}]},{"id":"blk-39694","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39696","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68494","marks":["bold"],"text":"static_config:"},{"id":"spn-68495","text":" none."}]}],"id":"blk-39695","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39698","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68496","marks":["bold"],"text":"ports:"},{"id":"spn-68497","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-68498","marks":["code"],"text":"sig_in"},{"id":"spn-68499","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-39697","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39700","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68500","marks":["bold"],"text":"state:"},{"id":"spn-68501","text":" "},{"id":"spn-68502","marks":["code"],"text":"open"},{"id":"spn-68503","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68504","marks":["code"],"text":"next_open"},{"id":"spn-68505","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-39699","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39702","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68506","marks":["bold"],"text":"invariant:"},{"id":"spn-68507","text":" "},{"id":"spn-68508","marks":["code"],"text":"open' = next_open"},{"id":"spn-68509","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-68510","marks":["code"],"text":"next_open' = incoming wire "},{"id":"spn-68511","text":".nxt`."}]}],"id":"blk-39701","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-39703","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68512","text":"SpinnerDecl"}]},{"id":"blk-39704","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39706","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68513","marks":["bold"],"text":"static_config:"},{"id":"spn-68514","text":" lane geometry "},{"id":"spn-68515","marks":["code"],"text":"(w, n)"},{"id":"spn-68516","text":", initial "},{"id":"spn-68517","marks":["code"],"text":"rotor4"},{"id":"spn-68518","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68519","marks":["code"],"text":"configurable"},{"id":"spn-68520","text":" permission (fixed | configurable)."}]}],"id":"blk-39705","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39708","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68521","marks":["bold"],"text":"ports:"},{"id":"spn-68522","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-68523","marks":["code"],"text":"sig_in"},{"id":"spn-68524","text":" (exactly one); out "},{"id":"spn-68525","marks":["code"],"text":"socket"},{"id":"spn-68526","text":" (exactly one)."}]}],"id":"blk-39707","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39710","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68527","marks":["bold"],"text":"state:"},{"id":"spn-68528","text":" "},{"id":"spn-68529","marks":["code"],"text":"rotor"},{"id":"spn-68530","text":" (Q-fixed lanes, runtime STATE)."}]}],"id":"blk-39709","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39712","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68531","marks":["bold"],"text":"invariant:"},{"id":"spn-68532","text":" exactly one sig-in + exactly one socket; fixed spinners REJECT runtime rotor writes (typed error); configurable accept "},{"id":"spn-68533","marks":["code"],"text":"SetRotor"},{"id":"spn-68534","text":" at COMMIT."}]}],"id":"blk-39711","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-39713","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68535","text":"OrbDecl"}]},{"id":"blk-39714","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39716","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68536","marks":["bold"],"text":"static_config:"},{"id":"spn-68537","text":" none."}]}],"id":"blk-39715","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39718","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68538","marks":["bold"],"text":"ports:"},{"id":"spn-68539","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-68540","marks":["code"],"text":"pose"},{"id":"spn-68541","text":" (via socket)."}]}],"id":"blk-39717","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39720","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68542","marks":["bold"],"text":"state:"},{"id":"spn-68543","text":" "},{"id":"spn-68544","marks":["code"],"text":"pose4"},{"id":"spn-68545","text":", sticky "},{"id":"spn-68546","marks":["code"],"text":"numeric_fault"},{"id":"spn-68547","text":" bit."}]}],"id":"blk-39719","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39722","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68548","marks":["bold"],"text":"invariant:"},{"id":"spn-68549","text":" controller exclusivity (≤ 1 socket); "},{"id":"spn-68550","marks":["code"],"text":"numeric_fault' = fault_base OR current_overflow"},{"id":"spn-68551","text":" where "},{"id":"spn-68552","marks":["code"],"text":"fault_base = 0 if ResetFault else old"},{"id":"spn-68553","text":" (a reset cannot hide a same-epoch overflow)."}]}],"id":"blk-39721","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-39723","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68554","marks":["bold"],"text":"Frozen:"},{"id":"spn-68555","text":" node envelope, the five role IDs, their config/port/state signatures, their invariants. "},{"id":"spn-68556","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not frozen:"},{"id":"spn-68557","text":" user-defined behaviors, mailboxes, supervision, generic behavior tables, dynamic role loading, the physical IC encoding of each state. New built-in roles are additive "},{"id":"spn-68558","marks":["bold"],"text":"v1.x"},{"id":"spn-68559","text":"; a general actor-behavior system stays Experimental."}]},{"id":"blk-39724","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68560","text":"2. Edge vocabulary (D2)"}]},{"id":"blk-39725","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68561","text":"Exactly two "},{"id":"spn-68562","marks":["bold"],"text":"structural topology edges"},{"id":"spn-68563","text":" are frozen:"}]},{"id":"blk-39726","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"SignalWireDecl    { src.sig_out → dst.sig_in }   ; dst ∈ {Door, Relay, Spinner}\nSocketControlDecl { spinner.socket → orb.pose }"},{"id":"blk-39727","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68564","text":"Legal pairs: "},{"id":"spn-68565","marks":["code"],"text":"(sig_out, sig_in)"},{"id":"spn-68566","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68567","marks":["code"],"text":"(socket, pose)"},{"id":"spn-68568","text":". Any other edge variant MUST fail validation."}]},{"id":"blk-39728","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68569","marks":["bold"],"text":"Graph edges are not transition classes."},{"id":"spn-68570","text":" These are NOT structural edge kinds in v1:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-39730","spans":[{"id":"spn-68571","text":"WRL texture"}]},{"id":"blk-39731","spans":[{"id":"spn-68572","text":"IR v1 status"}]}],"id":"blk-39729","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-39732","spans":[{"id":"spn-68573","text":"Solid "},{"id":"spn-68574","marks":["code"],"text":"--"}]},{"id":"blk-39733","spans":[{"id":"spn-68575","text":"executable through "},{"id":"spn-68576","marks":["code"],"text":"SignalWire"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39734","spans":[{"id":"spn-68577","text":"Async "},{"id":"spn-68578","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"}]},{"id":"blk-39735","spans":[{"id":"spn-68579","text":"reserved in WRL, "},{"id":"spn-68580","marks":["bold"],"text":"absent"},{"id":"spn-68581","text":" from IR v1 (no placeholder node)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39736","spans":[{"id":"spn-68582","text":"Verified "},{"id":"spn-68583","marks":["code"],"text":"=="}]},{"id":"blk-39737","spans":[{"id":"spn-68584","text":"acceptance machinery grounded; route construct "},{"id":"spn-68585","marks":["bold"],"text":"absent"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39738","spans":[{"id":"spn-68586","text":"Fault "},{"id":"spn-68587","marks":["code"],"text":"!!"}]},{"id":"blk-39739","spans":[{"id":"spn-68588","text":"fault state grounded; route/supervision construct "},{"id":"spn-68589","marks":["bold"],"text":"absent"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-39740","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68590","text":"A numeric-fault latch is "},{"id":"spn-68591","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-68592","text":" the lowering of a "},{"id":"spn-68593","marks":["code"],"text":"!!fault!!>"},{"id":"spn-68594","text":" route; an acceptance receipt is "},{"id":"spn-68595","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-68596","text":" a complete lowering of a "},{"id":"spn-68597","marks":["code"],"text":"==verified==>"},{"id":"spn-68598","text":" route. Reserved WRL syntax needs no placeholder canonical IR node."}]},{"id":"blk-39741","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68599","text":"3. State schema — semantic vs backend (D4)"}]},{"id":"blk-39742","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68600","text":"IR v1 freezes "},{"id":"spn-68601","marks":["bold"],"text":"semantic signatures"},{"id":"spn-68602","text":"; it excludes "},{"id":"spn-68603","marks":["bold"],"text":"backend encodings"},{"id":"spn-68604","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-39743","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68605","marks":["bold"],"text":"Semantic (in the artifact or a referenced policy/schema):"},{"id":"spn-68606","text":" signedness; lane width; fractional bits; numeric-policy identity; saturation behavior; rounding behavior; sticky-fault behavior; fixed-vs-configurable permission; fact/receipt capacity (when exhaustion is observable); rotor & pose lane counts; claim & receipt field meanings."}]},{"id":"blk-39744","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68607","marks":["bold"],"text":"Backend (excluded — belongs to a lowering profile):"},{"id":"spn-68608","text":" Scott encoding; tuple nesting; DUP labels; one-hot vs binary clock counter; packed-word layout; IC variable names; native struct padding; CUDA memory layout."}]},{"id":"blk-39745","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68609","marks":["bold"],"text":"Identity split (frozen):"}]},{"id":"blk-39746","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"SemanticArtifactID = hash( canonical Forge IR + semantic policy references )\nBackendArtifactID  = hash( SemanticArtifactID + lowering profile + compiler hash + backend representation )"},{"id":"blk-39747","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68610","text":"Changing one-hot → binary changes the "},{"id":"spn-68611","marks":["bold"],"text":"BackendArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-68612","text":" only (not the world identity or WorldFrame). Changing Q32.32 → Q16.16 changes the "},{"id":"spn-68613","marks":["bold"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-68614","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-39748","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68615","text":"4. Frozen top-level forms"}]},{"id":"blk-39749","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"ForgeSemanticArtifactV1 {\n    ir_version\n    profile_id                 ; \"forge.world.core.v1\" (deterministic-circuit-world)\n    semantic_policies {\n        rulepack_id\n        numeric_policy_ids\n        admit_policy_id        ; e.g. admit_candidate_min_firstreceipt_v1\n        film_schema_id\n    }\n    schemas {\n        runtime_state_schema\n        epoch_input_schema\n        observable_schema\n    }\n    objects: [ PulserDecl, RelayDecl, DoorDecl, SpinnerDecl, OrbDecl ]\n    edges:   [ SignalWireDecl, SocketControlDecl ]\n    initial_state\n}\n\nRuntimeStateV1 {\n    epoch\n    clock_states\n    signal_states\n    door_states\n    relay_states\n    spinner_rotors\n    orb_poses\n    numeric_faults\n    claim_facts\n    acceptance_receipts\n    capacity_faults\n}\n\nEpochInputV1 { claim_batch }          ; ClaimBatch of SetRotor|ResetFault envelopes\n\nEpochResultV1 { runtime_state, world_frame, ledger_entries }"},{"id":"blk-39750","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68616","text":"5. Transition law (frozen)"}]},{"id":"blk-39751","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68617","text":"Per epoch the transition is the WRL Core 0.1.1 cycle:"}]},{"id":"blk-39752","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"OBSERVE → ACCEPT → MAP → COMMIT → REACT → FILM"},{"id":"blk-39753","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68618","text":"For claim-free epochs OBSERVE/ACCEPT/MAP degenerate to identity but remain in the model. COMMIT applies MAP'd controls (SetRotor writes + fault resets) to owned cells; REACT runs the deterministic within-period token cascade to fixpoint and latches overflow; FILM emits the "},{"id":"spn-68619","marks":["bold"],"text":"WorldFrame"},{"id":"spn-68620","text":" (physical, Film v0.6 family) + "},{"id":"spn-68621","marks":["bold"],"text":"EventLedger"},{"id":"spn-68622","text":" entries (claim-aware, Film v0.7 family). Canonical ordering is policy-pinned (the ADMIT profile pins "},{"id":"spn-68623","marks":["code"],"text":"CandidateKey"},{"id":"spn-68624","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-39754","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68625","text":"6. Versioning (D5)"}]},{"id":"blk-39755","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39757","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68626","marks":["bold"],"text":"v1"},{"id":"spn-68627","text":" freezes on the grounded "},{"id":"spn-68628","marks":["code"],"text":"deterministic-circuit-world"},{"id":"spn-68629","text":" profile — sufficient evidence exists (multiple clock modes, randomized topologies, fan-in/out, cycles, multiple controllers, dynamic rotors, persistent multi-epoch state, claims/receipts, fault reset, pose authority, native+reference reducers). It does "},{"id":"spn-68630","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-68631","text":" claim to be the universal final Forge IR."}]}],"id":"blk-39756","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39759","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68632","marks":["bold"],"text":"v1.1"},{"id":"spn-68633","text":" — additive role/field variants when a second world family arrives."}]}],"id":"blk-39758","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39761","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68634","marks":["bold"],"text":"v1.x"},{"id":"spn-68635","text":" — additive optional feature declarations."}]}],"id":"blk-39760","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39763","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68636","marks":["bold"],"text":"v2"},{"id":"spn-68637","text":" — any change to the meaning of an existing field. A second implementation must NOT silently reinterpret v1 fields."}]}],"id":"blk-39762","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-39764","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68638","text":"7. First WRL vertical slice (what the compiler supports)"}]},{"id":"blk-39765","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"WRL Core text/canvas → canonical WRL graph → Forge Semantic IR v1\n    → current Fixture adapter → TRVM compiler → ic_ref / ic32 → Film v0.7"},{"id":"blk-39766","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68639","text":"Supported: Pulser, Relay, Door, Spinner, Orb; signal wires; socket control; fixed-point policy declarations; "},{"id":"spn-68640","marks":["code"],"text":"SetRotor"},{"id":"spn-68641","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-68642","marks":["code"],"text":"ResetFault"},{"id":"spn-68643","text":"; a fixed number of periods. Everything else → clear unsupported-feature diagnostic."}]},{"id":"blk-39767","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68644","text":"8. Conformance (what IR v1 does NOT define)"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-39769","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68645","text":"IR v1 defines static deterministic signal graphs containing the five built-in roles, persistent numeric pose state, bounded ADMIT claim state, and the two grounded topology relations. It does not define mailboxes, arbitrary actor behavior, dynamic topology, fragments, capabilities, supervision, or distributed settlement."}]}],"id":"blk-39768","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-39770","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68646","text":"D1–D5 resolution"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-39772","spans":[{"id":"spn-68647","text":"Decision"}]},{"id":"blk-39773","spans":[{"id":"spn-68648","text":"Ruling (frozen)"}]}],"id":"blk-39771","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-39774","spans":[{"id":"spn-68649","text":"D1 node vocabulary"}]},{"id":"blk-39775","spans":[{"id":"spn-68650","text":"stable node envelope + five closed built-in roles"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39776","spans":[{"id":"spn-68651","text":"D2 edge vocabulary"}]},{"id":"blk-39777","spans":[{"id":"spn-68652","text":"two structural edge kinds only; async/fault/verified are transition-class reserved, not edges"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39778","spans":[{"id":"spn-68653","text":"D3 ADMIT"}]},{"id":"blk-39779","spans":[{"id":"spn-68654","text":"static policy + top-level runtime ClaimState + separate EpochInput (three layers)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39780","spans":[{"id":"spn-68655","text":"D4 state schema"}]},{"id":"blk-39781","spans":[{"id":"spn-68656","text":"semantic signature frozen in artifact; physical representation excluded to backend profile; Semantic/Backend artifact-ID split"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39782","spans":[{"id":"spn-68657","text":"D5 freeze timing"}]},{"id":"blk-39783","spans":[{"id":"spn-68658","text":"freeze now as restricted "},{"id":"spn-68659","marks":["code"],"text":"deterministic-circuit-world"},{"id":"spn-68660","text":" profile; v1.1 additive, v2 semantic"}]}]]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieragdxphcaovkzozq2hlbpjbcaxxxilakq7cgie3dtmdm5uqotwd7ia","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}